* This PR is for [Issue #8](https://github.com/HLRichardson-Git/Gestalt/issues/8)

### Description of the Change

Adds the Data Encryption Standard (DES aka DEA) and Triple DES (aka TDEA) algorithms from [FIPS 46-3](https://csrc.nist.gov/files/pubs/fips/46-3/final/docs/fips46-3.pdf) & [FIPS SP 800-67r2](https://nvlpubs.nist.gov/nistpubs/SpecialPublications/NIST.SP.800-67r2.pdf)
 * DES_ECB
 * DES_CBC
 * 3DES_ECB
 * 3DES_CBC

These can all be uses by a user by including `#include <gestalt/des.h>`, here is an example of using 3DES_CBC:

```cpp
#include <gestalt/des.h>
#include <iostream>

int main() {
    const std::string key = "752878397493CB70";
    const std::string key2 = "10316E028C8F3B4A";
    const std::string key3 = "7CA110454A1A6E57";
    const std::string nonce = "0102030405060708";
    const std::string plaintext = "Hello, Gestalt!";

    std::string ciphertext = encrypt3DESECB(plaintext, key, key2, key3);

    std::cout << "3DES_CBC: " << ciphertext << std::endl;

    return 0;
}
```

Updates the following documentation:

* README
* CHANGES
* CONTRIBUTING

### Alternate Designs

Currently, the `src/modes` directory is where modes of operation for block cipher templates should be. Due to the difference in my AES and DES implementation, I was not able to get it to work. For now DESs modes of operation are defined independently in `gestalt/des.h`. It is planned in the next version `0.6.1` to rework AES and the modes templates to remedy this.

### Verification Process

I wrote a new suite of test vectors in `tests/desTests.cpp` that test the DES functions and diverse encrytion/ decryption cases. This provides confidence that the algorithms are correct, and if a code change is made in the future then the tests are already present.

### Release Notes

 * Adds DES-ECB/CBC
 * Adds 3DES-ECB/CBC
 * Fixes AES-CBC
 * Improves testing for AES

if a non-placeholder insert replaces the placeholder while another thread is executing a placeholder insert, it is possible for `PlaceholderGuard::insert_with_lifecycle` to drain and notify waiters, without setting `inserted` to true

when the guard is dropped, this will trigger `drop_slow`, which would in turn set the state to `LoadingState::Terminated`

if any of the previously notified waiters wakes after this point, it sees `LoadingState::Terminated` instead of `LoadingState::Inserted` and crashes with `unreachable!()` https://github.com/arthurprs/quick-cache/blob/544dc2cae13785cf798f8234e60124fa44774c67/src/sync_placeholder.rs#L168-L177

this repro consistently panics on my machine after a few iterations:

```rs
    #[tokio::test(flavor = "multi_thread")]
    async fn test_repro_panic() {
        use std::sync::{Arc, atomic::AtomicBool, atomic::Ordering};
        use std::time::Duration;

        loop {
            let cache = Arc::new(quick_cache::sync::Cache::<u64, u64>::new(1024 * 1024));
            let flag = Arc::new(AtomicBool::new(false));
            let mut tasks = vec![];

            for _i in 0..3 {
                let cache = cache.clone();
                let flag = flag.clone();
                tasks.push(tokio::spawn(async move {
                    match cache.get_value_or_guard_async(&0).await {
                        Ok(v) => println!("{v}"),
                        Err(guard) => {
                            tokio::time::sleep(Duration::from_millis(20)).await;
                            if flag.load(Ordering::Relaxed) {
                                let _ = guard.insert(1);
                            }
                        }
                    }

                    flag.store(true, Ordering::Relaxed);
                    tokio::time::sleep(Duration::from_millis(20)).await;
                    cache.insert(0, 0);
                }));
                tokio::time::sleep(Duration::from_micros(100)).await;
            }

            futures::future::join_all(tasks).await;
        }
    }
```

